## What this does

This PR does what the title says.

### Summary

The judge offered a prose unit per line, so a hard-wrapped commit message was 13 units of which 11 were mid-sentence fragments. A vote naming some of a paragraph's lines and not the rest left half a sentence behind.

A prose unit is now the markdown block. Unwrapped text is unaffected — a paragraph written on one line was always one unit — so what moves is hard-wrapped text: a commit message at 72 columns, and the four standards that wrap rather than the fourteen that do not.

`Co-Authored-By:` and every other git trailer is shown to the model as context and never offered. The prompt tells the model to delete provenance, and a trailer is exactly that.

### Testing

`go test ./...` passes; three cases cover the block rule and two the trailer rule.

I have carefully reviewed this change and I am confident it is correct.
